# {{SLUG}} agents

Config-only agent directories: each `agents/<id>/` holds a `manifest.json`, a
`site.yaml` validated against the reusable-agents schemas, an `AGENT.md`, and
3 to 7 goals bound to `RunResult.metrics`. The engines (price refresh, catalog
discovery, shelf audit, spec extraction, pick building, recall gate, goals
tracker, ...) live in reusable-agents; nothing here forks one.

- Create an agent with reusable-agents `install/create-agent.sh <id>
  {{SITE_DIR}}/agents ...` (see the reusable-agents CLAUDE.md, "Creating a new
  agent"). Ship every manifest with `"enabled": false` and no `cron_expr`
  until the operator approves it going live.
- `register-with-framework.sh` registers every directory here that has a
  manifest; run it only on the operator's go-ahead. The scaffold registers
  nothing.
- `implementer-scope.yaml` is the implementer block every per-site
  `site.yaml` that dispatches to the implementer must carry, and reusable-agents
  `examples/sites/{{SLUG}}.yaml` too (copy it in whole): it keeps `vendor/**`,
  `site.json`, `{{POLICY_FILE}}` and the gate policy (`tests/ui/gate.config.ts`)
  out of every dispatch kind, and the page manifest out of deploy repairs,
  but only where it is applied: on the implementer's framework-chain path and
  by the deployer to its repairs. The implementer's default claude path
  commits without any scope check (reusable-agents
  `agents/implementer/README.md`, "Path scope"), so there those files and the
  gate wiring are protected only by instructions. The deploy gate's kit
  checks (`tests/run-local-suite.sh`: the manifest, then the kit release in
  reusable-agents) catch an edited `vendor/affiliate-kit` only while the shim
  itself is untouched and the claimed kit version is committed in
  reusable-agents; nothing in this repository catches an edited `site.json`,
  policy or gate policy.
- **Prerequisite: keep this site's implementer dispatches disabled.** Register
  or enable no agent whose recommendations dispatch to the implementer for
  this site (the SEO opportunity agent, article proposals, head-to-heads,
  catalog audits) until either the implementer's claude path applies this
  scope to its own commits (reverting or refusing an excluded path), or the
  reusable-agents deployer refuses a release whose diff since the last green
  deploy touches an excluded path (reusable-agents
  `kits/affiliate-site/CHANGELOG.md`, "Known issues").
